BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//WebMS Intra//Test fixture//EN
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:What this proves: COUNT counts every date the rule produces, not just the
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:ones inside the window the portal asked for. This series starts on 1 August
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:2026, a month before the window, and asks for 40 daily dates - so it ends on
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:9 September 2026 and only the last nine dates (1 to 9 September) are inside
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:the window. A reader that counted only the dates it kept would carry on to
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:10 October and show 31 dates that were never in the calendar. A series that
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:began before the period being looked at is the ordinary case, not a rare one.
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:count-before-window-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260801T100000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260801T110000
RRULE:FREQ=DAILY;COUNT=40
SUMMARY:Daily for forty days
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
